// A program with ONE open obligation of its own: `100 / n` owes `n != 0`,
// and n is how many of seven numbers pass a filter, a count the compiler
// does not work out. Its compile surfaces exactly that one, never the
// runtime library's own open claims beside it (the frontier's user-link
// leg). It runs to 20.
fn inv(n) = 100 / n

fn big(x) = x > 2

fn main() = inv(len(filter(big, [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7])))
